{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 9b35d922ceacd247312222a7c17c26c037ff87c7, reporting artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:25e64920ddbd0529a222c0501962e4c0d69c763c, under request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:434b97fbe08a57ee73ce17fe4c2d2fdc18b2c58e and implementation promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c6b16251959e5158a39d57b8bfe9996a6070fdc2. I read the full fresh review request and corrected packet. This approval supersedes neither historical evidence nor the qualifications below. Both prior changes-requested verdicts are ratified. The current primary directly reports the live implementation promise, rests on the live landed note and the review findings, and has no describes_superseded_world flag. Ordinary inherited staleness was examined and is acknowledged.\n\nArchitecture: this changes layer 7 documentation about unchanged layer 2 kernel, layer 5 interpreter and layer 6 projection contracts. The sole changed note preserves the adopted Case C decline and does not change runtime, resolver or architecture contracts, so no architecture-page contract amendment is required. I compared the cited Folder.Projection and foldState.project function bodies across the historical and current code; they are unchanged. The final fold citations now identify the intended code at lines 539 and 3171.\n\nSecurity: I examined source provenance, URL/path handling and failure behavior. The twenty external citations are exact public-repository HTTPS commit links paired with bounded literal native source links. They introduce no secrets or new execution/authority boundary. Existing traversal refusal remains intact. This is the already assigned documentation correctness repair of the adopted decline, with unchanged conditions and authority; it does not commission a new authority-bearing implementation chain. No unresolved security defect found.\n\nSimplification: the head removes the twenty unavailable relative-link presentations and their explanatory workaround, keeping the existing paired citation pattern in one note. This meets both reading surfaces without changing the shared resolver or introducing exemptions. No further required simplification found.\n\nIndependent evidence: in my clean detached checkout of the exact head, Go 1.26.7 TestLocalMarkdownLinks passed (0.343s), and ./internal/docset/... passed (56.363s). An isolated missing-file negative control failed specifically on the nonexistent local path, proving that the root gate still detects missing files. I verified all twenty source links (eighteen unique) against exact Git blobs and line contents. I reran the actual React component in a Vite/JSDOM harness bound to current artifact 25e64920: twenty cited-line native clicks and twenty exact external anchors succeeded, with zero unavailable presentations; the introductory whole-file native link accounts for the twenty-first native anchor. This is component/JSDOM evidence, not a native-browser run. Twenty-one resident preview windows, including the committed note, were ready and source-equal when rebound to that same current artifact.\n\nI read the author's corrected renderer script and retained exit-zero log; the old harness's incorrect twenty-total expectation is explicitly corrected to twenty cited-line anchors plus one introductory file anchor. Author build, vet, docset and HTTPS checks are author evidence, not claimed as my own execution. Separately, I archived the exact merge-tree of current main 411681f17671311faea9d75767337973248e898b and this candidate (tree 014fb8221d88f405430530bcf46e3b5636eea4e6); Go 1.26.7 root Markdown gate passed (0.258s). I did not run a full combined suite.\n\nThe previous main CI failures for 0afa98aa, c8c29c69 and 411681f1 remain failures of the twenty original Case C links until this repair is sealed, pushed and a combined main run is green. The separate reading-view companion request git:sha1:5d262274